{"id":"granicus-1-1616","platform":"granicus","body":"City Council","name":"City Council Meeting","date":"2021-09-28","time":"","canceled":false,"agenda_url":"https://pvestates.granicus.com/AgendaViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=1616","minutes_url":"https://pvestates.granicus.com/MinutesViewer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=1616&doc_id=cb77a7aa-2627-11ec-88a7-0050569183fa","packet_url":"","clip_id":1616,"view_id":1,"video_url":"https://pvestates.granicus.com/MediaPlayer.php?view_id=1&clip_id=1616","transcript_url":"","mp4_url":"","mp3_url":"","agenda_text":"September 28, 2021\n12:15\nPM\nVia Zoom Teleconference\n340 Palos Verdes Drive West\nPalos Verdes Estates, CA 90274\nAGENDA\nOF A REGULAR MEETING\nOF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF\nPALOS VERDES ESTATES, CALIFORNIA 90274\nCopies of the staff reports or other written documentation relating to each item of business referred to on the agenda are on file in the office of the City Clerk and are available for public inspection. If applicable, materials related to an item on this agenda submitted to the Council after distribution of the agenda packet are available for public inspection in the City Clerk's office during normal business hours. Any person having any question concerning any agenda item may call the City Clerk to make inquiry concerning the item. Upon request, the agenda and documents in the agenda packet can be made available in appropriate alternative formats to persons with a disability in compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act. Please contact the City Clerk at 310-378-0383, at least 48 hours prior to the meeting to request a disability-related modification or accommodation.\nThe City Council welcomes and encourages public participation at the Council meetings; however, to allow for the orderly progression of business, each person wishing to comment or make a presentation shall be limited to up to three (3) minutes. Anyone wishing to address the City Council is requested to fill out a green speaker's card available at the entry of the meeting room. The card permits the City to identify persons for purposes of City Council minute preparation. Please see specific agenda sections below for any other requirements related to meeting participation. The City Council, at the direction of the Mayor with concurrence of the Council, may modify the order of items shown on the agenda.\nAny person having any question concerning any agenda item may call the City Clerk to make inquiry concerning the item. Upon request, the agenda and, if any, documents in the agenda packet can be made available in appropriate alternative formats to persons with a disability in compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act. Please contact the City Clerk at 310-378-0383, at least 24 hours prior to the meeting to request a disability-related modification or accommodation.\nThe City Council welcomes and encourages public participation at the Council meetings. This meeting will be held via videoconference only in order to reduce the risk of spreading COVID-19 and pursuant to the Governor's Executive Orders N-25-20 and N-29-20 and the County of Los Angeles Public Health Officer's Safer at Home Order (revised March 21, 2020). All votes taken during this teleconference meeting will be by roll call vote, and the vote will be publicly reported.\nHOW TO VIEW THE MEETING: No physical location from which members of the public may observe the meeting and offer public comment will be provided. The meeting will not be livestreamed; however, the meeting will be recorded and made available on the City's website. You may attend the meeting through a computer or telephone:\nBY COMPUTER: https://us02web.zoom.us/j/88965785478\nZoom Meeting ID: 889 6578 5478\nBY TELEPHONE: 1 669 900 9128, Enter Code: 889 6578 5478#\nHOW TO PARTICIPATE DURING THE MEETING: Members of the public are encouraged to participate under COMMUNICATIONS FROM THE PUBLIC or on any item of interest on the Agenda by simply utilizing the \"Raise Hand\" feature during the item under consideration. When called upon to speak please state your name for the record. Members of the public are not required to submit notification in advance. Public correspondence submitted electronically via email will be provided to the legislative body, but will not be read aloud at the meeting.?\nAgenda reports and other disclosable public documents relating to each Agenda Item are available on the City's website under City Council Meeting Agendas at www.pvestates.org.\nCALL TO ORDER\nPLEDGE OF ALLEGIANCE\nROLL CALL\nAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\nMAYOR’S REPORT - MATTERS OF COMMUNITY INTEREST\nCITY MANAGER'S REPORT\nCOMMUNICATIONS FROM THE PUBLIC\nThis portion of the agenda is reserved for comments from the public on items which are NOT on the agenda. Due to state law, no action can be taken by the Council this evening on matters presented under this section. If the Council determines action is warranted, the item may be referred to staff or placed on a future Council agenda.\nCONSENT AGENDA (ITEMS 1-10)\n1.\nCITY COUNCIL ACTION MINUTES\na)\nSeptember 8, 2021 Special Meeting\nb)\nSeptember 14, 2021 Special Meeting\nc)\nSeptember 14, 2021 Regular Meeting\nd)\nSeptember 15, 2021 Special Closed Session\ne)\nSeptember 20, 2021 Special Closed Session\nRecommendation: Review and Approve.\nMinutes\n2.\nAPPROVAL OF WARRANT REGISTERS\nRecommendation:   Review and Approve Warrant Register(s) for the months of August and September 28, 2021.\nWarrants\n3.\nRECEIPT AND FILING OF THE MONTHLY INVESTMENT TRANSACTION REPORTS FOR THE MONTHS ENDING JULY 31, 2021 AND AUGUST 31, 2021\nRecommendation: Receive and File the monthly Investment Reports for the months ending July 31, 2021 and August 31, 2021.\nTreasurer's Reports\n4.\nRECEIPT AND FILING OF FINANCIAL STATEMENTS FOR THE PERIODS ENDING JULY 31 AND AUGUST 31, 2021\nRecommendation: Staff recommends the City Council receive and file financial statements for the months ending July 31 and August 31, 2021.\nStaff Report\n5.\nAPPROVAL OF AGREEMENT FOR INTERIM CITY MANAGER SERVICES\nRecommendation: That the City Council Approve the Agreement for Interim City Manager Services, which provides that Sharon K. Papa will serve as the City’s Interim City Manager while the Council recruits a new City Manager.\nStaff Report\n6.\nEXTENSION OF AGREEMENT WITH MOTOROLA SOLUTIONS\nRecommendation: Approve a one-year extension of the agreement with Motorola Solutions to provide maintenance and support for the City’s police radio infrastructure equipment, mobiles, and portable radios in the amount of $45,800.00 during FY 2021/22 and authorize the Mayor to execute an amendment to extend the agreement.\nStaff Report\n7.\nPLANNING COMMISSION ACTIONS OF SEPTEMBER 21, 2021\nRecommendation: That the City Council receive and file.\nFinal Staff Report\n7. Correspondence\n8.\nACCEPTANCE OF DONATIONS\nRecommendation: That the City Council accept the donations from the Confidence Foundation, in the amount of $4,300.00, and from Phyllis Martin in the amount of $50.00 as presented and thank the donors for their generosity.\nStaff Report\n9.\nAPPROVAL OF SPECIAL EVENT APPLICATION SUBMITTED BY THE PENINSULA EDUCATION FOUNDATION FOR THEIR “TOAST ON THE COAST” FUNDRAISING EVENT TO BE HELD IN THE PASEO DEL MAR PARKING LOT ON NOVEMBER 5, 2021.\nRecommendation: That the City Council approve the Special Event Application submitted by the Peninsula Education Foundation for their “Toast on the Coast” fundraising event on Saturday, November 5, 2021.\nStaff Report\n10.\nTEMPORARY EXTENSION NO. 2 OF AGREEMENT WITH STAY GREEN, INC. FOR CITYWIDE LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE SERVICES TO OCTOBER 31, 2021\nRecommendation: That the City Council grant a second temporarily extension to the current one-year agreement with Stay Green, Inc. for citywide landscape maintenance services until October 31, 2021.\nStaff Report\nPUBLIC HEARING(S)/ORDINANCES\n11.\nORDINANCE NO. 021-751 OF THE CITY OF PALOS VERDES ESTATES, CALIFORNIA, AMENDING TITLE 10, VEHICLES AND TRAFFIC, OF THE PALOS VERDES ESTATES MUNICIPAL CODE BY ADDING CHAPTER 10.64 REGARDING OVERSIZED VEHICLES\nRecommendation: That the City Council introduce on first reading and read by Title only proposed Ordinance No. 021-751: An Ordinance of the City of Palos Verdes Estates, California Amending Title 10 Vehicles and Traffic, by Adding Chapter 10.64 Regarding Oversized Vehicles.\nStaff Report\nCorrespondence\nOLD BUSINESS\nNEW BUSINESS\n12.\nAPPROVAL OF A PROFESSIONAL SERVICES AGREEMENT FOR CITY MANAGER RECRUITMENT SERVICES\nRecommendation: (1) Consider the recommendation of Mayor Kemps and Mayor Pro Tem Lozzi relative to the selection of a firm to conduct a recruitment for the vacant City Manager position; and (2) Approve a professional services agreement with Ralph Anderson & Associates for Executive Search services.\nStaff Report\n13.\nAPPROVAL FOR THE AWARD OF A CONSTRUCTION CONTRACT FOR THE PW-686-21 FY 21/22 MISCELLANEOUS STREET REPAIRS PROJECT\nRecommendation: That the City Council (1) Award a construction contract to Onyx Paving Company, Inc. for the PW-686-21 FY 21/22 Miscellaneous Street Repairs Project in the amount of $137,000.00 and authorize a 10% contingency in the amount of $13,700.00; and (2) Authorize the Mayor to execute the construction contract on behalf of the City.\nStaff Report\nMAYOR AND COUNCILMEMBER REPORTS\nThis portion of the agenda is reserved for the Mayor and Councilmembers to provide comments, report on community activities and ad hoc committees, and propose topics to be calendared on a future Council agenda.\nFUTURE AGENDA ITEMS\nFuture Agenda Items\nADJOURNMENT TO TUESDAY, October 12, 2021 AT 6:30 P.M.\ni.\nThis City Council meeting can be viewed on demand thereafter on the City Website at www.pvestates.org.\nI hereby certify under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of California, that the foregoing agenda was posted on the City Hall Bulletin Boards located by front door located at 340 Palos Verdes Drive West, Palos Verdes Estates, CA 90274, not less than 72 hours prior to the meeting in accordance with Government Code Section 54954.2.  Dated this 23rd day of September, 2021.\nCarol Cowley, Interim City Clerk","minutes_text":"PK\u0003\u0004\u0014\u0000\u0006\u0000\b\u0000\u0000\u0000!\u0000/�\u0000%�\u0001\u0000\u0000�\u0007\u0000\u0000\u0013\u0000\b\u0002[Content_Types].xml �\u0004\u0002(�\u0000\u0002\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u000